<b>Performers'
Waiting Room</b>

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:35.410
At Sainan High?

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:36.800
Yeah, tomorrow.

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:38.220
I want to see it!

00:08:38.220 --> 00:08:42.400
But I'm recording a new song tomorrow.

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:44.040
It's fine, don't worry.

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:46.780
The speech isn't my real goal anyway.

00:08:46.780 --> 00:08:47.500
Hm?

00:08:48.410 --> 00:08:52.460
I'm going to thoroughly investigate your beloved Rito-kun for you!

00:08:53.750 --> 00:08:55.400
F-For me!?

00:08:56.050 --> 00:08:57.830
Thank you so much!

00:08:57.830 --> 00:08:59.050
Leave it to me!

00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:02.860
...and that's the library-

00:09:01.800 --> 00:09:02.860
Hey.

00:09:02.860 --> 00:09:04.640
What do you do on your days off?

00:09:06.280 --> 00:09:08.690
Nothing much.

00:09:08.690 --> 00:09:11.580
Basically clean the house or play games.

00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:12.820
Hm, hm.

00:09:12.820 --> 00:09:16.200
So basically you're free on your days off, then?

00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:18.960
Well, then.

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:22.040
The next time you have a day off,

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:24.250
would you like to go on a date with me?

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:28.330
W-What'd you just say?!

00:09:28.980 --> 00:09:30.290
It was a joke.

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:33.260
If I did that, Run would get angry with me.

00:09:35.270 --> 00:09:37.890
After all, you're Run's prince.

00:09:40.360 --> 00:09:41.510
I...

00:09:43.190 --> 00:09:44.680
He's turning red.

00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:46.990
He's naive, just like I thought.

00:09:46.990 --> 00:09:48.350
Kyouko-kun.

00:09:49.620 --> 00:09:52.480
Principal?!

00:09:52.480 --> 00:09:56.200
Thanks for your speech today.

00:09:56.730 --> 00:10:03.450
I'm grateful that you were able to
make time in your busy schedule for us.

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:05.620
Ah... Y-Yeah...

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:08.460
This guy really is the principal here...

00:10:08.890 --> 00:10:15.840
I'm sure our students have learned much about the world from your speech.

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:18.380
How wonderful.

00:10:18.380 --> 00:10:19.190
Huh?

00:10:19.190 --> 00:10:22.180
Could it be he's relatively normal at school?

00:10:22.180 --> 00:10:26.600
Learning is wonderful...{Wait for it...}

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:30.770
Please...

00:10:32.750 --> 00:10:35.170
Please include me as well!

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:39.460
Teach me all kinds of things... in private!{Teach me all kinds of things, with just the two of us!}

00:10:39.460 --> 00:10:40.530
I knew it!

00:10:41.170 --> 00:10:41.830
Geez!

00:10:41.830 --> 00:10:43.300
Why are you always like this?

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:44.990
Principal!

00:10:44.990 --> 00:10:49.660
We of the Public Morals Committee will not permit any actions that would bring shame on our school!

00:10:50.890 --> 00:10:53.710
Yuuki-kun, hurry and take Kirisaki-san somewhere safe.

00:10:53.710 --> 00:10:54.970
G-Got it!

00:10:54.970 --> 00:10:56.420
Thank you!

00:10:56.900 --> 00:10:58.300
Thank you, Kotegawa!

00:10:58.740 --> 00:11:01.510
It's not like I'm doing it for your sake.

00:11:06.130 --> 00:11:07.680
{Can't hear what the students yelling at the principal are saying, all 5 overlap}

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:11.880
I wonder if I should have said I
always watch Magical Kyouko?

00:11:15.690 --> 00:11:18.250
Ah, we're safe.{we're saved.}

00:11:18.250 --> 00:11:20.820
I'm sorry about the principal.

00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:24.520
There's nothing for you to really apologise for, Rito-kun.

00:11:30.310 --> 00:11:31.440
Kyouko-san.

00:11:31.440 --> 00:11:32.120
Again?!

